1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:01,820
Who started Tesla?

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,660
Elon Musk, right?

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:04,600
Wrong.

4
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,180
It's 2003.

5
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,740
Two engineers, Martin Eberhard and Marc

6
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:11,060
Tarpenning, have a crazy idea.

7
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:13,400
An electric car that's actually cool.

8
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,060
They named the company after the

9
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,640
inventor, Nikola Tesla.

10
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:18,300
But they had one problem.

11
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:19,180
Money.

12
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:21,940
Then in 2004, a young billionaire

13
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:22,860
walks in.

14
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:23,820
Elon Musk.

15
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:26,400
He invests millions, becomes chairman, starts

16
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,440
taking control.

17
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,140
But here's the crazy part.

18
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:31,880
In 2007, Eberhard, the man who

19
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:33,340
started it all, was pushed out

20
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:34,820
of his own company.

21
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:36,800
He sued, and the settlement said

22
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,940
Musk could officially call himself a

23
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:39,640
co-founder.

24
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:42,440
So today, almost everyone believes Musk

25
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,100
built Tesla from the start, but

26
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,420
the real founders?

27
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:47,540
Most people have never heard their

28
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:48,140
names.

